# Backend API Development Context

## What This Is
FastAPI backend for rMirror Cloud - handles uploads, OCR processing, Notion sync, and data storage.

## Tech Stack
- **Framework**: FastAPI with async/await
- **Database**: PostgreSQL (production), SQLite (local dev)
- **ORM**: SQLAlchemy 2.0
- **Migrations**: Alembic (always use `poetry run alembic`)
- **Package Manager**: Poetry (always use `poetry run` for all commands)
- **Queue**: SyncQueue table with background worker
- **OCR**: Google Gemini (`ocr_model`, default `gemini-2.5-flash`; `GOOGLE_AI_API_KEY`), `app/core/ocr_service.py`
- **Auth**: Clerk only (session tokens; 30-day agent JWT from `POST /auth/agent-token`). Password login endpoints were removed
- **Deployment**: Hetzner VPS (<server-ip>) via GitHub Actions (push to `main` = staging, production = manual workflow)

## Key Architecture Patterns
- **Two-phase sync**: Phase 1 (metadata) creates notebook/page stubs instantly, Phase 2 (content) uploads .rm files with OCR
- **NOT_SYNCED status**: Page stubs created by metadata sync, awaiting content upload
- **Background sync worker**: Asyncio-based worker (app/services/sync_worker.py) polls queue every 5s; the same loop also rebuilds dirty notebook PDFs, sends drip emails and runs retroactive OCR for `PENDING_QUOTA` pages (app/jobs/process_pending_pages.py, a few users/pages per poll, one worker per user via a Postgres advisory lock)
- **Blocking calls off the loop**: sync SDK calls (Gemini, boto3, Notion SDK, rsvg-convert) are wrapped with `run_off_loop` from app/utils/concurrency.py
- **Database-driven deduplication**: SyncRecord table tracks what's synced (not Notion-based)
- **Upsert pattern**: Query by page identifier (`page_uuid`), update content_hash
- **Content hashing**: SHA-256 for change detection, stored in database only

## Critical Files
- `app/main.py`: FastAPI app, lifespan events, sync worker startup
- `app/models/`: SQLAlchemy models (Notebook, Page, NotebookPage; SyncQueue, SyncRecord and IntegrationConfig all live in `sync_record.py`)
- `app/api/`: Route handlers organized by resource
- `app/services/sync_worker.py`: Background worker for sync queue processing
- `app/integrations/notion_sync.py`: Notion sync implementation
- `app/core/sync_engine.py`: `SyncTarget` base class, `SyncItem`, `ContentFingerprint`
- `app/services/quota_service.py`: quota functions (module-level, no class)
- `app/utils/concurrency.py`: `run_off_loop`

## Database Schema (Key Tables)
- `users`: User accounts
- `subscriptions`: User subscriptions (tier, status, billing periods, Stripe IDs)
- `quota_usage`: OCR quota tracking (limit, used, reset_at by user and quota type `ocr`)
- `notebooks`: reMarkable notebooks (uuid, visible_name, parent_uuid)
- `pages`: Notebook pages (page_uuid is nullable and NOT unique, ocr_text, ocr_status, file_hash)
- `notebook_pages`: Page order per notebook (notebook_id, page_id, page_number)
- `sync_queue`: Pending sync tasks (item_type `page_text`/`todo`, content_hash, target_name, status, priority)
- `sync_records`: Sync history (external_id = Notion block ID, content_hash for change detection, unique on page_uuid + target_name + user_id)
- `integration_configs`: User integration settings (target_name, config_encrypted, is_enabled)

